 {'idx': 75, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'region of the main belt, but rather unusual in the inner parts. "Pink Floyd" has an absolute magnitude of 14.6. As of 2017, no rotational lightcurve of "Pink Floyd" has been obtained from photometric observations. The asteroid\'s rotation period, spin axis and shape remain unknown. This minor planet was named after the English rock band Pink Floyd, which released several astronomically themed songs such as "Interstellar Overdrive" and "Astronomy Domine". The bands album "The Dark Side of the Moon" (1973) became one of the best-selling records of all time. The official naming citation was published by the Minor Planet Center', 'title': '19367 Pink Floyd'}
