 {'idx': 9, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': '(1967) opens with a clearly audible Dm7 suspension. Carole King\'s song "I Feel the Earth Move" from her album "Tapestry" (1971) features a striking B chord at the end of the phrase "mellow as the month of May". Another example can be found in the piece "One Short Day", part of the musical "Wicked" by Stephen Schwartz, which starts with a descending arpeggio of a suspended chord. In rock, the verse of The Who song "Pinball Wizard" is a sequence of suspended fourth chords resolving to their major counterparts (B – B – A – A etc.). Two examples of', 'title': 'Suspended chord'}
