 {'idx': 5, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'L. Devoma Sangguniang Barangay Members: San Isidro, Cabuyao Barangay San Isidro (PSGC: 043404015) is one of the 18 urbanized barangays, comprising the city of Cabuyao in the province of Laguna, Philippines. It is located around three kilometers from Cabuyao City proper, along the national highway. According to the 2010 Census, it has a population of 18,145 (having increased from 15,495 in Census 2007), making it the 5th largest barangay in Cabuyao by population. The barangay got its name from its patron saint, San Isidro Labrador. According to 2010 Census, it has a population of 18,145 inhabitants, decreased from 15,495 in', 'title': 'San Isidro, Cabuyao'}
