 {'idx': 12, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Survivor Philippines (season 1) The first season of "Survivor Philippines" premiered on September 15, 2008, and ended its run on December 14 of the same year. Auditions for this season were held in six Philippine cities in May 2008. From these auditions, 18 contestants (up from the originally announced 16) were selected to participate on the show in June 2008. The show was shot in Ko Tarutao, the same island where "" took place, from July to August, 2008. The names of the tribes were derived from the Thai language: "Naak" (นาค), "Jarakay" (จระเข้) and "Chalam" (ฉลาม), meaning "snake", "crocodile"', 'title': 'Survivor Philippines (season 1)'}]

