 {'idx': 10, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Ten Nights in a Bar Room (1910 film) Ten Nights in a Bar Room is a 1910 American silent short drama produced by the Thanhouser Company. Adapted from the novel "Ten Nights in a Bar-Room and What I Saw There" by Timothy Shay Arthur, the production focuses on Joe Morgan after he has become a hopeless drunkard. Often Morgan\'s young daughter, Mary, comes to beg her father to return home. One day, she appears during a fight between the two men and is fatally struck by a bottle thrown by the saloon-keeper. Before Mary dies she asks her father to', 'title': 'Ten Nights in a Bar Room (1910 film)'}
