 {'idx': 30, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': "Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt The Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt () was a State of the Holy Roman Empire, ruled by a younger branch of the House of Hesse. It was formed in 1567 following the division of the Landgraviate of Hesse between the four sons of Landgrave Philip I. The residence of the landgraves was in Darmstadt, hence the name. As a result of the Napoleonic Wars, the landgraviate was elevated to the Grand Duchy of Hesse following the Empire's dissolution in 1806. The landgraviate comprised the southern Starkenburg territory with the Darmstadt residence and the northern province of Upper Hesse with", 'title': 'Landgraviate of Hesse-Darmstadt'}
