 {'idx': 12, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Essen-Dellwig station Essen-Dellwig station is located in the city of Essen in the German state of North Rhine-Westphalia on the Duisburg–Dortmund railway, opened by the Cologne-Minden Railway Company on 15 May 1847. The station opened between 1880 and 1897. It is classified by Deutsche Bahn as a category 6 station. The station is located 300m away from Essen-Dellwig Ost station. The station is served by line S 2 (running between Dortmund and Duisburg, operating every 60 minutes during the day. It is also served by tram lines 103 of the Essen Stadtbahn, operated at 10-minute intervals and bus routes 166', 'title': 'Essen-Dellwig station'}
