 {'idx': 7, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Gaius Norbanus Flaccus (consul 24 BC) Gaius Norbanus Flaccus (fl. 1st century BC) was a Roman senator who was appointed Roman consul in 24 BC. A member of the Nobiles, Flaccus was the son of Gaius Norbanus Flaccus, who had been consul in 38 BC. The father possessed a good relationship with Augustus, and this connection was continued with the younger Flaccus. In 24 BC, he was elected as consul, with Augustus as his colleague. In either 18/17 or 17/16 BC, he was appointed the proconsular governor of Asia. Flaccus was also a member of the "Quindecimviri sacris faciundis". Flaccus', 'title': 'Gaius Norbanus Flaccus (consul 24 BC)'}
