 {'idx': 11, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Sergei Vorzhev Sergei Vorzhev (Russian: "Сергей Дмитриевич Воржев;" born 21 February 1950) is a Russian artist based in Krasnodar. Sergei Dmitrievich Vorzhev was born on 21 February 1950 in Varenikovskaya cossack village of Krasnodar Region. In 1972 he graduated from the Faculty of Art of Kuban State University. He is a member of the Russia\'s Painters union since 1983. In the subjects of his works he falls back upon the history of Kuban, represents landscapes and wild nature of his smaller motherland, applying very often the ethnic surrealism style. One of his favorite motives is the marapatsutsa ("my solar chariot").', 'title': 'Sergei Vorzhev'}
