 {'idx': 4, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Manny Mashouf Manny Mashouf (born 6 July 1938) is an Iranian-American businessman and philanthropist known for founding Bebe Stores. Born in Iran in 1938, he came to the United States in his teens and settled first in Washington D.C., then in San Francisco. There, he went to San Francisco State University and graduated with a political science degree. He first managed a steakhouse, before founding his own fashion line. He was the manager and chairman of Bebe stores. In 1998, he took the company public. In 2006 Mashouf was worth US$1.5 billion - resulting in Forbes listing him as the', 'title': 'Manny Mashouf'}
