 {'idx': 30, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Michael V. Smith Michael V. Smith is a Canadian novelist, poet and filmmaker, originally from Cornwall, Ontario and now living in Kelowna, British Columbia. His debut novel, "Cumberland", was nominated for the Books in Canada First Novel Award in 2002. He has also been a nominee for the Journey Prize and the inaugural winner of the Dayne Ogilvie Prize, and has published two books of poetry, "What You Can\'t Have" and "Body of Text", and a memoir, "My Body Is Yours". Smith, openly gay, is a graduate of the University of British Columbia\'s Creative Writing program. He has also made', 'title': 'Michael V. Smith'}
