 {'idx': 15, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Alessandro Lualdi Alessandro Lualdi J.C.D. S.T.D. (12 August 1858 - 12 November 1927) was a Roman Catholic Cardinal who served as Archbishop of Palermo. Lualdi was born in Milan, Italy. He entered the Seminary of Milan and carried on further studies at the Theological Academy of Saint Thomas Aquinas in Rome where he earned doctorates in theology, philosophy and canon law. He was ordained in 1880. After his ordination, he worked in the Archdiocese of Milan doing pastoral work from 1884 until 1890. He later served as a Faculty member of the Seminary of Milan until 1894. He was created', 'title': 'Alessandro Lualdi'}
