 {'idx': 17, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Hybart, Alabama Hybart is an unincorporated community in Monroe County, in the U.S. state of Alabama. Hybart (pronounced "Hibbert") is located at (31.826506, -87.382094). It is located at the intersection of Alabama State Route 41 and Monroe County Road 56, in the northwestern part of Monroe County, just a short distance from its border with Wilcox County, Alabama. Hybart is the host of a locally famous Alabama turkey hunting competition called the Butterball which has appeared in "Mobile Bay Magazine". The area is also known for being a good hunting spot for whitetail deer, turkey, quail, dove, and duck. Hybart', 'title': 'Hybart, Alabama'}
