 {'idx': 5, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': "Afrikaner Party The Afrikaner Party (AP) was a South African political party from 1941 to 1951. The Afrikaner Party's roots can be traced back to September 1939, when South Africa declared war on Germany shortly after the start of World War II. The then Prime Minister J.B.M. Hertzog and his followers did not agree with this move and broke away from the United Party to form the Volksparty (People's Party). The Volksparty later split: one faction joined the Gesuiwerde Nasionale Party (Purified National Party) to form the Herenigde Nasionale Party (Re-united National Party) while the other faction became the Afrikaner", 'title': 'Afrikaner Party'}
