 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Doctors\' plot The Doctors\' plot (, "doctors\' case", also known as the case of doctors-saboteurs (врачи-вредители) or doctors-killers (врачи-убийцы)) was an antisemitic campaign organized by Joseph Stalin. In 1952–1953, a group of predominantly Jewish doctors from Moscow were accused of conspiring to assassinate Soviet leaders. This was later accompanied by publications of anti-Semitic character in the media, which talked about the threats of Zionism and condemned people with Jewish names. Many doctors, officials and others, both Jews and non-Jews, were promptly dismissed from their jobs and arrested. A few weeks after the death of Stalin, the new Soviet leadership stated', 'title': "Doctors' plot"}
