 {'idx': 6, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Buried at Milton Cemetery, Milton, MA and his tombstone was designed by his friends Stanford White and Augustus Saint-Gaudens. See here: Platt and other friends organized a memorial exhibition at the St. Botolph Club, held in 1891. The paintings of Bunker\'s early maturity in New York (ca. 1880-82) were often marine subjects, featuring a series of beached boats, painted on Long Island. In these he followed the standard academic practice of first painting loose, preparatory sketches ("Beached", ca. 1881-2) prior to more conventionally finished exhibition pieces. The early portraits ("Portrait of Walter Griffin", 1881, Portland Museum of Art) also evidence', 'title': 'Dennis Miller Bunker'}
