 {'idx': 7, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': "Altaír Tejeda de Tamez Altaír Tejeda de Tamez (Ciudad Victoria, Tamaulipas, Mexico; October 23, 1922 – September 17 2015) was a Mexican short story writer, poet, playwright and journalist. Altaír Tejeda Treviño was born on October 23, 1922 in Ciudad Victoria, Tamaulipas, Mexico, to Rafael Tejeda Puente and Elvira Treviño, both of them professors. She studied at the Leona Vicario elementary school, and made her secondary studies at the Normal and Preparatory School of Tamaulipas, finishing her studies at the Teacher's National School in Mexico City as Elementary School Professor. She went on to study a master's degree in Spanish", 'title': 'Altaír Tejeda de Tamez'}
