 {'idx': 6, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Ragusa was included in 1808 AD), and later in the Illyrian Provinces from 1809 AD. After the final defeat of Napoleon, the entire territory was granted to the Austrian Empire by the Congress of Vienna in 1815 AD. Venetian Dalmatia was inhabited by autochthonous Romance-speaking peoples and by Slavic-speaking peoples (who arrived in Dalmatia after 640 AD). The Romance population spoke the Dalmatian language and Venetian language, and also Italian language and Latin language. The Slavic population spoke archaic dialects of what is today known as Serbo-Croatian. The Dalmatian population adhered to Roman Catholicism in the maritime areas and in', 'title': 'Venetian Dalmatia'}
