 {'idx': 19, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'the 2,105th most common surname in the US, with 15,000 people (0.006%) sharing the surname. Luke (name) Luke is a male given name, and less commonly, a surname. The name Luke is the English form of the Latin name . It is derived from the Latin name "Lucius", and it either means "the great Lucius", or it is a shortened form of the Latin name. "Lucius" means "the bright one" or "the one born at dawn". The frequently stated explanation of as "man from Lucania" is not supported by reliable sources. Although the name is attested in ancient inscriptions, the', 'title': 'Luke (name)'}
