 {'idx': 3, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': '1923. Frank Silver explained the origin of the song to "Time Magazine": "I am an American, of Jewish ancestry, with a wife and a young son. About a year ago my little orchestra was playing at a Long Island hotel. To and from the hotel I was wont to stop at a fruit stand owned by a Greek, who began every sentence with \'Yess.\' The jingle of his idiom haunted me and my friend Cohn. Finally I wrote this verse and Cohn fitted it with a tune." Silver may have been influenced by an actual shortage of Gros Michel bananas', 'title': 'Yes! We Have No Bananas'}
