 {'idx': 2, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Sir Richard Everard, 2nd Baronet Sir Richard Everard, 2nd Baronet (1625 - 29 August 1694) was an English politician who sat in the House of Commons from 1661 to 1679. Everard was the son of Sir Richard Everard, 1st Baronet of Much Waltham, Essex and his first wife Joan Barrington, daughter of Sir Francis Barrington, 1st Baronet and his wife Joan Cromwell, daughter of Sir Henry Cromwell. In 1661, he was elected Member of Parliament for Westminster in the Cavalier Parliament. He succeeded to the Baronetcy about 1680. Everard died at the age of 69, and was buried at Waltham.', 'title': 'Sir Richard Everard, 2nd Baronet'}
