 {'idx': 34, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Dolev–Yao model The Dolev–Yao model is a formal model used to prove properties of interactive cryptographic protocols. The network is represented by a set of abstract machines that can exchange messages. These messages consist of formal terms. These terms reveal some of the internal structure of the messages, but some parts will hopefully remain opaque to the adversary. The adversary in this model can overhear, intercept, and synthesize any message and is only limited by the constraints of the cryptographic methods used. In other words: "the attacker carries the message." This omnipotence has been very difficult to model and many', 'title': 'Dolev–Yao model'}
