 {'idx': 26, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Solving chess Solving chess means finding an optimal strategy for playing chess, i.e. one by which one of the players (White or Black) can always force a victory, or both can force a draw (see Solved game). It also means more generally solving "chess-like" games (i.e. combinatorial games of perfect information), such as infinite chess. According to Zermelo\'s theorem, a hypothetically determinable optimal strategy does exist for chess and chess-like games. In a weaker sense, "solving chess" may refer to proving which one of the three possible outcomes (White wins; Black wins; draw) is the result of two perfect players,', 'title': 'Solving chess'}
