[{'idx': 0, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Jar of Flies Jar of Flies is the third studio EP by the American rock band Alice in Chains, released on January 25, 1994, through Columbia Records. It is the first EP in music history to debut at number one on the "Billboard" 200 Chart with the first week sales exceeding 141,000 copies in the United States. The EP was well received by critics and has since been certified triple-platinum by the RIAA and has gone on to sell 4 million copies worldwide, making "Jar of Flies" one of the band\'s most successful releases. In Japan, the EP is titled', 'title': 'Jar of Flies'}
 {'idx': 1, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'four guys getting together in the studio and making some music." Columbia Records released Alice in Chains\' second acoustic-based EP, "Jar of Flies", on January 25, 1994. Written and recorded in one week, "Jar of Flies" debuted at number one on the "Billboard" 200, becoming the first EP—and first Alice in Chains release—to top the charts. Paul Evans of "Rolling Stone" called the EP "darkly gorgeous", and Steve Huey said, "\'Jar of Flies\' is a low-key stunner, achingly gorgeous and harrowingly sorrowful all at once". "Jar of Flies" features Alice in Chains\' first number-one single on the Mainstream Rock charts,', 'title': 'Alice in Chains'}
