 {'idx': 9, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Sakurako Ohara Ohara likes western songs with catchy, upbeat melody. She also likes many Japanese songs with good lyrics. The first CD she bought was Annie\'s theme song "Tomorrow". The first time she sang a Japanese song in front of other people was when she was in her first year of elementary school: during the birthday of her mom, she sang BoA\'s "Every Heart -Minna no kimochi-". The first song she sang in English was the theme song "Part of your world" from the movie "The little mermaid". Ohara\'s talents include dancing, piano, ballet, singing, swimming, imitating. Ohara being a', 'title': 'Sakurako Ohara'}
