 {'idx': 9, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'La Liga play-offs The La Liga play-offs are an annual series of football matches to determine the final promotion places within Segunda División and La Liga. In its current format, it involves the four teams that finish directly below the automatic promotion places from Segunda División to the top tier. These teams meet in a series of play-off matches to determine the final team that will be promoted. Reserve teams are not eligible for promotion. The play-offs were first introduced in 1929 and have been staged at the conclusion of every season since. Until 1999, it consisted in games between', 'title': 'La Liga play-offs'}
