 {'idx': 10, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Bliss (yacht) Bliss is a super-yacht launched on the 5th of May 2014 at the Palmer Johnson shipyard in Sturgeon Bay and delivered the next year. The interior and exterior design of "Bliss" were done by Nuvolari & Lenard. She is currently not available for charter. "Bliss" has one sistership named DB9. A second sistership named "Sanam", built in Florida, was delivered in July 2016. The length of the yacht is and the beam is . The draught of "Bliss" is . Both the materials of the hull and the superstructure are made out of Aluminium with teak laid decks.', 'title': 'Bliss (yacht)'}
