 {'idx': 11, 'is_supporting': False, 'paragraph_text': 'Charmaine (song) "Charmaine" is a popular song written by Ernö Rapée and Lew Pollack. The song was written in 1926 and published in 1927. However, Desmond Carrington on his BBC Radio 2 programme marked the song\'s writing as being in 1913. The song was originally in waltz time, but later versions were in common time. The song was originally composed for the 1926 silent movie "What Price Glory?", and most notably, the best-selling version, recorded by Guy Lombardo & his Orchestra, spent seven weeks at the #1 position in 1927. It was also featured in the movie "Two Girls and', 'title': 'Charmaine (song)'}]

