[{'idx': 0, 'is_supporting': True, 'paragraph_text': 'Timpani Timpani (; ) or kettledrums (also informally called timps) are musical instruments in the percussion family. A type of drum, they consist of a membrane called a head stretched over a large bowl traditionally made of copper. Most modern timpani are "pedal timpani" and can be tuned quickly and accurately to specific pitches by skilled players through the use of a movable foot-pedal. They are played by striking the head with a specialized drum stick called a "timpani stick" or "timpani mallet". Timpani evolved from military drums to become a staple of the classical orchestra by the last third', 'title': 'Timpani'}
